    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (the other two are a base and a helper), and it passes. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the owner resource so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `\"initials\": \"J.S.\"` for an owner named \"john smith\".\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this spec at build time, alongside the existing `displayName`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `initials` via a MapStruct expression backed by a new `initials(Owner)` default method that returns the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`). `firstName`/`lastName` are `@NotEmpty`, so `charAt(0)` is safe for any persisted owner.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreComputesInitials` passes and the suite is green.",
